  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The clearest candidate is dependency caching (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE), but this workflow already caches pip via actions/setup-python@v5 with cache: \"pip\", which stores the same ~/.cache/pip directory that the evidence example caches with actions/cache@v4. The pattern's contraindication \"An equivalent cache already exists\" therefore applies, and adding a duplicate cache step would be redundant rather than an improvement. No other supported pattern fits: there is no matrix (so P-LIT-FAIL-FAST / P-LIT-FAILED-JOB-FIRST do not apply), no schedule (so P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE / P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE do not apply), path filters are already declared (P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER is already satisfied), all three test steps are required checks so test selection/skipping (P-LIT-SELECT, P-LIT-PRIORITIZE, P-LIT-UNAFFECTED-STEPS) would reduce coverage, and there is no Bazel build (P-LIT-BAZEL-*). Applying any of these would either duplicate existing caching, weaken required-check coverage, or be unrelated to this workflow.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
}
